@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment] independent-service-roles
Marshall and Lilly MUST be independently enabled. Enabled services MUST reject
incomplete configuration. Neither serving role may run database migrations at
startup; ADR-0036's separate updater may migrate before activating a candidate.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] module-runtime-secrets
Plaintext credential options MUST name private runtime files outside the Nix
store, never literal secret values. Marshall MUST run unprivileged and receive
only its application credentials, without access to the host SSH or age private
identities.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] module-guest-lifetime
Lilly MUST retain host mount visibility. VM units MUST occupy a separate slice
from the daemon and survive its restart. Service activation MUST NOT repartition,
destroy storage, replace host identity or kill independently running guests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] module-ipv4-service-sandboxes
Maintained service address-family allowlists MUST NOT permit AF_INET6. Local
Unix, vsock and Netlink families remain independent of IPv4 network transport.
